# No em or en dashes

Never use em dashes (—) or en dashes (–) in new user-facing text, docs, comments, emails, grant copy, commit messages, or chat replies for this project.

Use plain alternatives:

| Instead of | Use |
|---|-----|
| clause — clause | period, semicolon, colon, comma, or parentheses |
| 2026–2027 | 2026-2027 (hyphen) |
| pages 12–15 | pages 12-15 (hyphen) |
| Leo — Addon | Leo (Addon) or Leo Addon |

ASCII hyphen-minus `-` is fine for compound words, date ranges, and markdown list markers. Markdown thematic breaks (`---`) are fine.

Existing files may still contain em/en dashes; do not introduce new ones. When editing prose the user is actively preparing to send or submit, strip them.
